  ('PILOT', 'Psalm 48:14', 'For this God is our God for ever and ever; he will be our guide even to the end.', NOW()),
  ('PLANT', '1 Corinthians 3:6', 'I planted the seed, Apollos watered it, but God has been making it grow.', NOW()),
  ('POWER', 'Acts 1:8', 'But you will receive power when the Holy Spirit comes on you; and you will be my witnesses in Jerusalem, and in all Judea and Samaria, and to the ends of the earth.', NOW()),
  ('GODLY', '1 Timothy 4:8', 'For physical training is of some value, but godliness has value for all things, holding promise for both the present life and the life to come.', NOW()),
  ('PRICE', '1 Corinthians 6:20', 'You were bought at a price. Therefore honor God with your bodies.', NOW()),
  ('PRIDE', 'Proverbs 11:2', 'When pride comes, then comes disgrace, but with humility comes wisdom.', NOW()),
  ('PROOF', '2 Timothy 3:16', 'All Scripture is God-breathed and is useful for teaching, rebuking, correcting and training in righteousness.', NOW()),
  ('PROSE', 'Psalm 150:6', 'Let everything that has breath praise the LORD. Praise the LORD.', NOW()),
  ('PROUD', 'James 4:6', 'But he gives us more grace. That is why Scripture says: God opposes the proud but shows favor to the humble.', NOW()),
  ('PROVE', 'Romans 12:2', 'Then you will be able to test and approve what God''s will is — his good, pleasing and perfect will.', NOW()),
  ('PRUNE', 'John 15:2', 'He cuts off every branch in me that bears no fruit, while every branch that does bear fruit he prunes so that it will be even more fruitful.', NOW()),
  ('PURGE', 'Psalm 51:7', 'Cleanse me with hyssop, and I will be clean; wash me, and I will be whiter than snow.', NOW()),
  ('RAISE', 'John 6:40', 'For my Father''s will is that everyone who looks to the Son and believes in him shall have eternal life, and I will raise them up at the last day.', NOW()),
  ('REACH', 'Philippians 3:14', 'I press on toward the goal to win the prize for which God has called me heavenward in Christ Jesus.', NOW()),
  ('READS', 'Revelation 1:3', 'Blessed is the one who reads aloud the words of this prophecy.', NOW()),
  ('READY', 'Matthew 24:44', 'So you also must be ready, because the Son of Man will come at an hour when you do not expect him.', NOW()),
  ('REAPS', 'Galatians 6:7', 'Do not be deceived: God cannot be mocked. A man reaps what he sows.', NOW()),
  ('SCORN', 'Psalm 44:13', 'You have made us the scorn of our neighbors, the derision and mockery of those around us.', NOW()),
  ('ATONE', 'Leviticus 16:30', 'Because on this day atonement will be made for you, to cleanse you. Then, before the LORD, you will be clean from all your sins.', NOW()),
  ('REPAY', 'Romans 12:19', 'Do not take revenge, my dear friends, but leave room for God''s wrath, for it is written: It is mine to avenge; I will repay, says the LORD.', NOW()),
  ('WEEPS', 'Luke 19:41', 'As he approached Jerusalem and saw the city, he wept over it.', NOW()),
  ('RESTS', 'Isaiah 11:2', 'The Spirit of the LORD will rest on him — the Spirit of wisdom and of understanding.', NOW()),
  ('RENEW', 'Isaiah 40:31', 'But those who hope in the LORD will renew their strength. They will soar on wings like eagles.', NOW()),
  ('GIFTS', 'Romans 11:29', 'For God''s gifts and his call are irrevocable.', NOW()),
  ('RIGHT', 'Psalm 19:8', 'The precepts of the LORD are right, giving joy to the heart.', NOW()),
  ('ROOTS', 'Colossians 2:7', 'Rooted and built up in him, strengthened in the faith as you were taught, and overflowing with thankfulness.', NOW()),
  ('ROYAL', '1 Peter 2:9', 'But you are a chosen people, a royal priesthood, a holy nation, God''s special possession.', NOW()),
  ('RULES', 'Psalm 103:19', 'The LORD has established his throne in heaven, and his kingdom rules over all.', NOW()),
  ('SAVED', 'Ephesians 2:8', 'For it is by grace you have been saved, through faith — and this is not from yourselves, it is the gift of God.', NOW()),
  ('SEALS', 'Ephesians 4:30', 'And do not grieve the Holy Spirit of God, with whom you were sealed for the day of redemption.', NOW()),
  ('SENDS', 'John 3:17', 'For God did not send his Son into the world to condemn the world, but to save the world through him.', NOW()),
  ('SHEDS', 'Romans 5:5', 'And hope does not put us to shame, because God''s love has been poured out into our hearts through the Holy Spirit.', NOW()),
  ('SHINE', 'Matthew 5:16', 'In the same way, let your light shine before others, that they may see your good deeds and glorify your Father in heaven.', NOW()),
  ('SIGNS', 'John 20:30', 'Jesus performed many other signs in the presence of his disciples, which are not recorded in this book.', NOW()),
  ('SIMON', 'Mark 1:17', 'Come, follow me, Jesus said, and I will send you out to fish for people.', NOW()),
  ('SINGS', 'Zephaniah 3:17', 'The LORD your God is with you, the Mighty Warrior who saves. He will take great delight in you; in his love he will no longer rebuke you, but will rejoice over you with singing.', NOW()),
  ('SLEEP', 'Psalm 4:8', 'In peace I will lie down and sleep, for you alone, LORD, make me dwell in safety.', NOW()),
  ('SMALL', 'Zechariah 4:10', 'Who dares despise the day of small things?', NOW()),
  ('SOLID', 'Hebrews 5:14', 'But solid food is for the mature, who by constant use have trained themselves to distinguish good from evil.', NOW()),
  ('SONGS', 'Ephesians 5:19', 'Speaking to one another with psalms, hymns, and songs from the Spirit. Sing and make music from your heart to the Lord.', NOW()),
  ('SPEAK', 'Jeremiah 1:7', 'But the LORD said to me, Do not say, I am too young. You must go to everyone I send you to and say whatever I command you.', NOW()),
  ('SPEND', 'Isaiah 55:2', 'Why spend money on what is not bread, and your labor on what does not satisfy?', NOW()),
  ('SPIRE', 'Genesis 11:4', 'Then they said, Come, let us build ourselves a city, with a tower that reaches to the heavens.', NOW()),
  ('SPLIT', 'Exodus 14:21', 'Then Moses stretched out his hand over the sea, and all that night the LORD drove the sea back.', NOW()),
  ('STOOD', 'Acts 7:55', 'But Stephen, full of the Holy Spirit, looked up to heaven and saw the glory of God, and Jesus standing at the right hand of God.', NOW()),
  ('STORE', 'Malachi 3:10', 'Bring the whole tithe into the storehouse, that there may be food in my house.', NOW()),
  ('STRAP', 'Luke 3:16', 'I am not worthy to untie the strap of his sandals.', NOW()),
  ('STRAY', 'Isaiah 53:6', 'We all, like sheep, have gone astray, each of us has turned to our own way.', NOW()),
  ('SWEAR', 'Matthew 5:37', 'All you need to say is simply Yes or No; anything beyond this comes from the evil one.', NOW()),
  ('SWEAT', 'Luke 22:44', 'And being in anguish, he prayed more earnestly, and his sweat was like drops of blood falling to the ground.', NOW()),
  ('TAKEN', 'Isaiah 53:8', 'By oppression and judgment he was taken away. Yet who of his generation protested?', NOW()),
  ('TEARS', 'Revelation 21:4', 'He will wipe every tear from their eyes. There will be no more death or mourning or crying or pain.', NOW()),
  ('THANK', '1 Thessalonians 5:18', 'Give thanks in all circumstances; for this is God''s will for you in Christ Jesus.', NOW()),
  ('THINE', 'Matthew 6:13', 'For yours is the kingdom and the power and the glory forever. Amen.', NOW()),
  ('THORN', '2 Corinthians 12:9', 'But he said to me, My grace is sufficient for you, for my power is made perfect in weakness.', NOW()),
  ('THREE', 'Matthew 28:19', 'Therefore go and make disciples of all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit.', NOW()),
  ('THROW', 'Psalm 55:22', 'Cast your cares on the LORD and he will sustain you; he will never let the righteous be shaken.', NOW()),
  ('TIDES', 'Psalm 93:4', 'Mightier than the thunder of the great waters, mightier than the breakers of the sea — the LORD on high is mighty.', NOW()),
  ('TOILS', 'Matthew 6:28', 'And why do you worry about clothes? See how the flowers of the field grow. They do not labor or spin.', NOW()),
  ('TORAH', 'Psalm 1:2', 'But whose delight is in the law of the LORD, and who meditates on his law day and night.', NOW()),
  ('TOUCH', 'Mark 5:28', 'Because she thought, If I just touch his clothes, I will be healed.', NOW()),
  ('TOWNS', 'Luke 4:43', 'But he said, I must proclaim the good news of the kingdom of God to the other towns also, because that is why I was sent.', NOW()),
  ('TRAIN', 'Proverbs 22:6', 'Start children off on the way they should go, and even when they are old they will not turn from it.', NOW()),
  ('TRIBE', 'Revelation 5:5', 'See, the Lion of the tribe of Judah, the Root of David, has triumphed.', NOW()),
  ('TRIES', 'Psalm 17:3', 'Though you probe my heart, though you examine me at night and test me, you will find that I have planned no evil.', NOW()),
  ('TYING', 'Mark 11:2', 'Go to the village ahead of you, and just as you enter it, you will find a colt tied there.', NOW()),
  ('UNION', 'Ephesians 4:3', 'Make every effort to keep the unity of the Spirit through the bond of peace.', NOW()),
  ('UNITY', 'Psalm 133:1', 'How good and pleasant it is when God''s people live together in unity!', NOW()),
  ('UNTIL', 'Philippians 1:6', 'Being confident of this, that he who began a good work in you will carry it on to completion until the day of Christ Jesus.', NOW()),
  ('OATHS', 'Hebrews 6:17', 'Because God wanted to make the unchanging nature of his purpose very clear to the heirs of what was promised, he confirmed it with an oath.', NOW()),
  ('VALID', 'John 8:17', 'In your own Law it is written that the testimony of two witnesses is true.', NOW()),
  ('VALOR', 'Joshua 1:9', 'Have I not commanded you? Be strong and courageous. Do not be afraid; do not be discouraged.', NOW()),
  ('VERSE', 'Psalm 119:11', 'I have hidden your word in my heart that I might not sin against you.', NOW()),
  ('VEXED', 'Psalm 6:3', 'My soul is in deep anguish. How long, LORD, how long?', NOW()),
  ('VINES', 'John 15:5', 'I am the vine; you are the branches. If you remain in me and I in you, you will bear much fruit.', NOW()),
  ('VOICE', 'John 10:27', 'My sheep listen to my voice; I know them, and they follow me.', NOW()),
  ('VOWED', 'Numbers 30:2', 'When a man makes a vow to the LORD or takes an oath to obligate himself by a pledge, he must not break his word.', NOW()),
  ('WALKS', 'Micah 6:8', 'And what does the LORD require of you? To act justly and to love mercy and to walk humbly with your God.', NOW()),
  ('WALLS', 'Nehemiah 4:6', 'So we rebuilt the wall till all of it reached half its height, for the people worked with all their heart.', NOW()),
  ('WANTS', '1 Timothy 2:4', 'Who wants all people to be saved and to come to a knowledge of the truth.', NOW()),
  ('WASTE', 'Isaiah 58:12', 'Your people will rebuild the ancient ruins and will raise up the age-old foundations.', NOW()),
  ('WAVES', 'Matthew 14:29', 'Then Peter got down out of the boat, walked on the water and came toward Jesus.', NOW()),
  ('WEARS', 'Colossians 3:12', 'Therefore, as God''s chosen people, holy and dearly loved, clothe yourselves with compassion, kindness, humility, gentleness and patience.', NOW()),
  ('WEARY', 'Isaiah 40:31', 'But those who hope in the LORD will renew their strength. They will soar on wings like eagles; they will run and not grow weary, they will walk and not be faint.', NOW()),
  ('WELLS', 'Isaiah 12:3', 'With joy you will draw water from the wells of salvation.', NOW()),
  ('WHOLE', 'Deuteronomy 6:5', 'Love the LORD your God with all your heart and with all your soul and with all your strength.', NOW()),
  ('WILLS', 'Matthew 6:10', 'Your kingdom come, your will be done, on earth as it is in heaven.', NOW()),
  ('WINDS', 'Psalm 104:4', 'He makes winds his messengers, flames of fire his servants.', NOW()),
  ('WINGS', 'Psalm 91:4', 'He will cover you with his feathers, and under his wings you will find refuge; his faithfulness will be your shield and rampart.', NOW()),
  ('WINES', 'John 2:10', 'And he said to him, Everyone serves the good wine first, and when people have drunk freely, then the poor wine. But you have kept the good wine until now.', NOW()),
  ('WISER', 'Proverbs 9:9', 'Instruct the wise and they will be wiser still; teach the righteous and they will add to their learning.', NOW()),
  ('WITTY', 'Proverbs 8:12', 'I, wisdom, dwell together with prudence; I possess knowledge and discretion.', NOW()),
  ('WOMEN', 'Luke 8:3', 'And Joanna the wife of Chuza, the manager of Herod''s household; Susanna; and many others. These women were helping to support them out of their own means.', NOW()),
  ('WORDS', 'Psalm 19:14', 'May these words of my mouth and this meditation of my heart be pleasing in your sight, LORD, my Rock and my Redeemer.', NOW()),
  ('WORKS', 'Ephesians 2:10', 'For we are God''s handiwork, created in Christ Jesus to do good works, which God prepared in advance for us to do.', NOW()),
  ('WORLD', 'John 3:16', 'For God so loved the world that he gave his one and only Son.', NOW()),
  ('WORRY', 'Matthew 6:34', 'Therefore do not worry about tomorrow, for tomorrow will worry about itself. Each day has enough trouble of its own.', NOW()),
  ('WORTH', 'Romans 8:18', 'I consider that our present sufferings are not worth comparing with the glory that will be revealed in us.', NOW()),
  ('WOUND', 'Isaiah 53:5', 'But he was pierced for our transgressions, he was crushed for our iniquities; the punishment that brought us peace was on him, and by his wounds we are healed.', NOW()),
  ('WRITE', 'Habakkuk 2:2', 'Then the LORD replied: Write down the revelation and make it plain on tablets so that a herald may run with it.', NOW()),
  ('YOUNG', 'Psalm 119:9', 'How can a young person stay on the path of purity? By living according to your word.', NOW()),
  ('YOURS', 'Psalm 24:1', 'The earth is the LORD''s, and everything in it.', NOW()),
  ('SOBER', '1 Peter 5:8', 'Be sober-minded; be watchful. Your adversary the devil prowls around like a roaring lion, seeking someone to devour.', NOW()),
  ('ZEALS', 'Numbers 25:13', 'He and his descendants will have a covenant of a lasting priesthood, because he was zealous for the honor of his God.', NOW())
ON CONFLICT (word) DO NOTHING;

-- M-02: Word bank expansion — Phase 10 critical fix.
-- Adds ~150 additional biblical words to reduce word repetition risk.
-- All entries are idempotent via ON CONFLICT (word) DO NOTHING.
INSERT INTO manna_words (word, scripture_reference, scripture_text, created_at) VALUES
  -- Biblical names
  ('AARON', 'Exodus 4:14', 'Then the LORD''s anger burned against Moses and he said, What about your brother, Aaron the Levite? I know he can speak well.', NOW()),
  ('ABNER', '2 Samuel 2:8', 'Meanwhile, Abner son of Ner, the commander of Saul''s army, had taken Ish-Bosheth son of Saul and brought him over to Mahanaim.', NOW()),
  ('ACHAN', 'Joshua 7:20', 'Achan replied, It is true! I have sinned against the LORD, the God of Israel. This is what I have done.', NOW()),
  ('ANNAS', 'Luke 3:2', 'During the high-priesthood of Annas and Caiaphas, the word of God came to John son of Zechariah in the wilderness.', NOW()),
  ('ASHER', 'Genesis 49:20', 'Asher''s food will be rich; he will provide delicacies fit for a king.', NOW()),
  ('CYRUS', 'Isaiah 45:1', 'This is what the LORD says to his anointed, to Cyrus, whose right hand I take hold of to subdue nations before him.', NOW()),
  ('DAGON', '1 Samuel 5:4', 'But the following morning when they rose, there was Dagon, fallen on his face on the ground before the ark of the LORD!', NOW()),
  ('ELIAM', '2 Samuel 23:34', 'Eliphelet son of Ahasbai the Maakathite, Eliam son of Ahithophel the Gilonite.', NOW()),
  ('ENOCH', 'Genesis 5:24', 'Enoch walked faithfully with God; then he was no more, because God took him away.', NOW()),
  ('ETHAN', 'Psalm 89:1', 'A maskil of Ethan the Ezrahite. I will sing of the LORD''s great love forever; with my mouth I will make your faithfulness known through all generations.', NOW()),
  ('FELIX', 'Acts 24:24', 'Several days later Felix came with his wife Drusilla. He sent for Paul and listened to him as he spoke about faith in Christ Jesus.', NOW()),
  ('GAIUS', '3 John 1:2', 'Dear friend, I pray that you may enjoy good health and that all may go well with you, even as your soul is getting along well.', NOW()),
  ('HAGAR', 'Genesis 21:17', 'God heard the boy crying, and the angel of God called to Hagar from heaven and said to her, What is the matter, Hagar? Do not be afraid.', NOW()),
  ('HEROD', 'Matthew 2:16', 'When Herod realized that he had been outwitted by the Magi, he was furious, and he gave orders to kill all the boys in Bethlehem.', NOW()),
  ('HIRAM', '1 Kings 5:12', 'The LORD gave Solomon wisdom, just as he had promised him. There were peaceful relations between Hiram and Solomon, and the two of them made a treaty.', NOW()),
  ('JABAL', 'Genesis 4:20', 'Adah gave birth to Jabal; he was the father of those who live in tents and raise livestock.', NOW()),
  ('JASON', 'Acts 17:6', 'But when they did not find them, they dragged Jason and some other believers before the city officials, shouting: These men who have caused trouble all over the world have now come here.', NOW()),
  ('JOASH', '2 Kings 12:2', 'Joash did what was right in the eyes of the LORD all the years Jehoiada the priest instructed him.', NOW()),
  ('JUBAL', 'Genesis 4:21', 'His brother''s name was Jubal; he was the father of all who play stringed instruments and pipes.', NOW()),
  ('KEZIA', 'Job 42:14', 'The first daughter he named Jemimah, the second Keziah and the third Keren-Happuch.', NOW()),
  ('KORAH', 'Numbers 16:31', 'As soon as he finished saying all this, the ground under them split apart and the earth opened its mouth and swallowed them.', NOW()),
  ('LABAN', 'Genesis 29:10', 'When Jacob saw Rachel daughter of his uncle Laban, and Laban''s sheep, he went over and rolled the stone away from the mouth of the well.', NOW()),
  ('LYDIA', 'Acts 16:14', 'One of those listening was a woman from the city of Thyatira named Lydia, a dealer in purple cloth. The Lord opened her heart to respond to Paul''s message.', NOW()),
  ('MAMRE', 'Genesis 18:1', 'The LORD appeared to Abraham near the great trees of Mamre while he was sitting at the entrance to his tent in the heat of the day.', NOW()),
  ('MERAB', '1 Samuel 14:49', 'Saul''s sons were Jonathan, Ishvi and Malki-Shua. The name of his older daughter was Merab, and that of the younger was Michal.', NOW()),
  ('MESHA', '2 Kings 3:4', 'Now Mesha king of Moab raised sheep, and he had to pay the king of Israel a tribute of a hundred thousand lambs.', NOW()),
  ('MICAH', 'Micah 6:8', 'He has shown you, O mortal, what is good. And what does the LORD require of you? To act justly and to love mercy and to walk humbly with your God.', NOW()),
  ('NABAL', '1 Samuel 25:3', 'His name was Nabal and his wife''s name was Abigail. She was an intelligent and beautiful woman, but her husband was surly and mean in his dealings.', NOW()),
  ('PALTI', 'Numbers 13:9', 'From the tribe of Benjamin, Palti son of Raphu.', NOW()),
  ('PEREZ', 'Genesis 38:29', 'But when he drew back his hand, his brother came out, and she said, So this is how you have broken out! And he was named Perez.', NOW()),
  ('RAHAB', 'Hebrews 11:31', 'By faith the prostitute Rahab, because she welcomed the spies, was not killed with those who were disobedient.', NOW()),
  ('REUEL', 'Exodus 2:18', 'When the girls returned to Reuel their father, he asked them, Why have you returned so early today?', NOW()),
  ('REZIN', '2 Kings 15:37', 'In those days the LORD began to send Rezin king of Aram and Pekah son of Remaliah against Judah.', NOW()),
  ('RUFUS', 'Romans 16:13', 'Greet Rufus, chosen in the Lord, and his mother, who has been a mother to me, too.', NOW()),
  ('SARAH', 'Genesis 17:15', 'God also said to Abraham, As for Sarai your wife, you are no longer to call her Sarai; her name will be Sarah.', NOW()),
  ('SARAI', 'Genesis 12:11', 'As he was about to enter Egypt, he said to his wife Sarai, I know what a beautiful woman you are.', NOW()),
  ('TEMAN', 'Habakkuk 3:3', 'God came from Teman, the Holy One from Mount Paran. His glory covered the heavens and his praise filled the earth.', NOW()),
  ('TIMON', 'Acts 6:5', 'This proposal pleased the whole group. They chose Stephen, a man full of faith and of the Holy Spirit; also Philip, Procorus, Nicanor, Timon, Parmenas, and Nicolas.', NOW()),
  ('URIAH', '2 Samuel 11:11', 'Uriah said to David, The ark and Israel and Judah are staying in tents, and my commander Joab and my lord''s men are camped in the open country.', NOW()),
  ('ZIMRI', '1 Kings 16:18', 'When Zimri saw that the city was taken, he went into the citadel of the royal palace and set the palace on fire around him. So he died.', NOW()),
  -- Biblical places
  ('BABEL', 'Genesis 11:9', 'That is why it was called Babel — because there the LORD confused the language of the whole world. From there the LORD scattered them over the face of the whole earth.', NOW()),
  ('BEZER', 'Deuteronomy 4:43', 'The cities were: Bezer in the wilderness plateau, for the Reubenites; Ramoth in Gilead, for the Gadites; and Golan in Bashan, for the Manassites.', NOW()),
  ('ENDOR', '1 Samuel 28:7', 'Saul then said to his attendants, Find me a woman who is a medium, so I may go and inquire of her. There is one in Endor, they said.', NOW()),
  ('GAZER', '1 Chronicles 14:16', 'So David did as God commanded him, and they struck down the Philistine army, all the way from Gibeon to Gazer.', NOW()),
  ('GOLAN', 'Deuteronomy 4:43', 'Golan in Bashan was one of the cities of refuge, set apart for the Manassites.', NOW()),
  ('HAZOR', 'Joshua 11:10', 'At that time Joshua turned back and captured Hazor and put its king to the sword. Hazor had been the head of all these kingdoms.', NOW()),
  ('HOREB', 'Exodus 17:6', 'I will stand there before you by the rock at Horeb. Strike the rock, and water will come out of it for the people to drink.', NOW()),
  ('JAFFA', 'Acts 9:36', 'In Joppa there was a disciple named Tabitha. She was always doing good and helping the poor.', NOW()),
  ('JOPPA', 'Jonah 1:3', 'But Jonah ran away from the LORD and headed for Tarshish. He went down to Joppa, where he found a ship bound for that port.', NOW()),
  ('KEDAR', 'Isaiah 60:7', 'All Kedar''s flocks will be gathered to you, the rams of Nebaioth will serve you; they will be accepted as offerings on my altar.', NOW()),
  ('LYCIA', 'Acts 27:5', 'When we had sailed across the open sea off the coast of Cilicia and Pamphylia, we landed at Myra in Lycia.', NOW()),
  ('MARAH', 'Exodus 15:23', 'When they came to Marah, they could not drink its water because it was bitter. That is why the place is called Marah.', NOW()),
  ('NEGEB', 'Genesis 12:9', 'Then Abram set out and continued toward the Negev, through the dry southern lands.', NOW()),
  ('OPHIR', '1 Kings 9:28', 'His men went to Ophir and brought back 420 talents of gold, which they delivered to King Solomon.', NOW()),
  ('PETRA', 'Matthew 16:18', 'And I tell you that you are Peter, and on this rock I will build my church, and the gates of Hades will not overcome it.', NOW()),
  ('RAMAH', 'Jeremiah 31:15', 'A voice is heard in Ramah, mourning and great weeping, Rachel weeping for her children and refusing to be comforted, because they are no more.', NOW()),
  ('SODOM', 'Genesis 19:24', 'Then the LORD rained down burning sulfur on Sodom and Gomorrah — from the LORD out of the heavens.', NOW()),
  ('TABOR', 'Judges 4:6', 'She sent for Barak and said to him, Go, take with you ten thousand men of Naphtali and Zebulun and lead them up to Mount Tabor.', NOW()),
  ('TAMAR', 'Genesis 38:11', 'Judah then said to his daughter-in-law Tamar, Live as a widow in your father''s household until my son Shelah grows up.', NOW()),
  ('TEKOA', 'Amos 1:1', 'The words of Amos, one of the shepherds of Tekoa — the vision he saw concerning Israel two years before the earthquake.', NOW()),
  ('TROAS', 'Acts 16:11', 'From Troas we put out to sea and sailed straight for Samothrace, and the next day we went on to Neapolis.', NOW()),
  ('ZORAH', 'Judges 13:2', 'A certain man of Zorah, named Manoah, from the clan of the Danites, had a wife who was childless, unable to give birth.', NOW()),
  -- Theological and spiritual words
  ('ABODE', 'John 14:23', 'Anyone who loves me will obey my teaching. My Father will love them, and we will come to them and make our home with them.', NOW()),
  ('ABYSS', 'Revelation 9:1', 'The fifth angel sounded his trumpet, and I saw a star that had fallen from the sky to the earth. The star was given the key to the shaft of the Abyss.', NOW()),
  ('ADOPT', 'Romans 8:15', 'The Spirit you received does not make you slaves, so that you live in fear again; rather, the Spirit you received brought about your adoption to sonship.', NOW()),
  ('AGAPE', 'John 13:35', 'By this everyone will know that you are my disciples, if you love one another.', NOW()),
  ('AGONY', 'Luke 22:44', 'And being in anguish, he prayed more earnestly, and his sweat was like drops of blood falling to the ground.', NOW()),
  ('AHAVA', 'Ezra 8:15', 'I assembled them at the canal that flows toward Ahava, and we camped there three days while I checked among the people and the priests.', NOW()),
  ('ALIVE', 'Romans 6:11', 'In the same way, count yourselves dead to sin but alive to God in Christ Jesus.', NOW()),
  ('ALLOT', 'Numbers 26:55', 'Be sure that the land is distributed by lot. What each group inherits will be according to the names for its ancestral tribe.', NOW()),
  ('ALONE', 'Matthew 14:23', 'After he had dismissed them, he went up on a mountainside by himself to pray. Later that night, he was there alone.', NOW()),
  ('ALPHA', 'Revelation 1:8', 'I am the Alpha and the Omega, says the Lord God, who is, and who was, and who is to come, the Almighty.', NOW()),
  ('ALTAR', 'Genesis 8:20', 'Then Noah built an altar to the LORD and, taking some of all the clean animals and clean birds, he sacrificed burnt offerings on it.', NOW()),
  ('AMBER', 'Ezekiel 1:4', 'I looked, and I saw a windstorm coming out of the north — an immense cloud with flashing lightning surrounded by brilliant light. The center of the fire looked like glowing metal.', NOW()),
  ('AMNON', '2 Samuel 3:2', 'Sons were born to David in Hebron: His firstborn was Amnon the son of Ahinoam of Jezreel.', NOW()),
  ('ARIEL', 'Isaiah 29:1', 'Woe to you, Ariel, Ariel, the city where David settled! Add year to year and let your cycle of festivals go on.', NOW()),
  ('AROMA', 'Ephesians 5:2', 'Walk in the way of love, just as Christ loved us and gave himself up for us as a fragrant offering and sacrifice to God.', NOW()),
  ('AWOKE', 'Genesis 28:16', 'When Jacob awoke from his sleep, he thought, Surely the LORD is in this place, and I was not aware of it.', NOW()),
  ('BARAK', 'Hebrews 11:32', 'And what more shall I say? I do not have time to tell about Gideon, Barak, Samson and Jephthah, about David and Samuel and the prophets.', NOW()),
  ('BARNS', 'Luke 12:18', 'Then he said, This is what I''ll do. I will tear down my barns and build bigger ones, and there I will store my surplus grain.', NOW()),
  ('BASIN', 'John 13:5', 'After that, he poured water into a basin and began to wash his disciples'' feet, drying them with the towel that was wrapped around him.', NOW()),
  ('BEARS', '1 Corinthians 13:7', 'It always protects, always trusts, always hopes, always perseveres.', NOW()),
