  ('HIDES', 'Psalm 119:11', 'I have hidden your word in my heart that I might not sin against you.', NOW()),
  ('HOLDS', 'Isaiah 41:13', 'For I, the LORD your God, hold your right hand; it is I who say to you, Fear not, I am the one who helps you.', NOW()),
  ('HONOR', 'Romans 12:10', 'Be devoted to one another in love. Honor one another above yourselves.', NOW()),
  ('HOPED', 'Hebrews 11:13', 'All these people were still living by faith when they died. They did not receive the things promised; they only saw them and welcomed them from a distance.', NOW()),
  ('HOUSE', 'Psalm 23:6', 'Surely your goodness and love will follow me all the days of my life, and I will dwell in the house of the LORD forever.', NOW()),
  ('HUMBLY', 'Micah 6:8', 'He has shown you, O mortal, what is good. And what does the LORD require of you? To act justly and to love mercy and to walk humbly with your God.', NOW()),
  ('IMAGE', 'Genesis 1:27', 'So God created mankind in his own image, in the image of God he created them; male and female he created them.', NOW()),
  ('INCENSE', 'Revelation 8:4', 'The smoke of the incense, together with the prayers of God''s people, went up before God from the angel''s hand.', NOW()),
  ('IRONS', 'Psalm 107:16', 'For he breaks down gates of bronze and cuts through bars of iron.', NOW()),
  ('ISAAC', 'Genesis 22:2', 'Then God said, Take your son, your only son, whom you love — Isaac — and go to the region of Moriah.', NOW()),
  ('JACOB', 'Genesis 32:28', 'Then the man said, Your name will no longer be Jacob, but Israel, because you have struggled with God and with humans and have overcome.', NOW()),
  ('JOYFUL', 'Psalm 98:4', 'Shout for joy to the LORD, all the earth, burst into jubilant song with music.', NOW()),
  ('JUDAH', 'Genesis 49:10', 'The scepter will not depart from Judah, nor the ruler''s staff from between his feet, until he to whom it belongs shall come.', NOW()),
  ('JUDGE', 'Genesis 18:25', 'Will not the Judge of all the earth do right?', NOW()),
  ('KEEPS', 'Psalm 121:4', 'Indeed, he who watches over Israel will neither slumber nor sleep.', NOW()),
  ('KNEEL', 'Philippians 2:10', 'That at the name of Jesus every knee should bow, in heaven and on earth and under the earth.', NOW()),
  ('KNOWN', 'Galatians 4:9', 'But now that you know God — or rather are known by God — how is it that you are turning back to those weak and miserable forces?', NOW()),
  ('LABORS', 'Revelation 14:13', 'Blessed are the dead who die in the Lord from now on. They will rest from their labor, for their deeds will follow them.', NOW()),
  ('LAMPS', 'Matthew 25:4', 'The wise ones, however, took oil in jars along with their lamps.', NOW()),
  ('LANDS', 'Psalm 22:27', 'All the ends of the earth will remember and turn to the LORD, and all the families of the nations will bow down before him.', NOW()),
  ('LATER', 'John 13:7', 'Jesus replied, You do not realize now what I am doing, but later you will understand.', NOW()),
  ('LEARN', 'Matthew 11:29', 'Take my yoke upon you and learn from me, for I am gentle and humble in heart, and you will find rest for your souls.', NOW()),
  ('LEAVE', 'Ruth 1:16', 'Where you go I will go, and where you stay I will stay. Your people will be my people and your God my God.', NOW()),
  ('LEAPS', 'Psalm 18:29', 'With your help I can advance against a troop; with my God I can scale a wall.', NOW()),
  ('LENDS', 'Psalm 37:26', 'They are always generous and lend freely; their children will be a blessing.', NOW()),
  ('LIFTS', 'Psalm 3:3', 'But you, LORD, are a shield around me, my glory, the One who lifts my head high.', NOW()),
  ('LIGHT', 'John 8:12', 'I am the light of the world. Whoever follows me will never walk in darkness, but will have the light of life.', NOW()),
  ('LIONS', 'Daniel 6:22', 'My God sent his angel, and he shut the mouths of the lions.', NOW()),
  ('LIVES', 'Galatians 2:20', 'I have been crucified with Christ and I no longer live, but Christ lives in me.', NOW()),
  ('LOFTY', 'Isaiah 57:15', 'For this is what the high and exalted One says — he who lives forever, whose name is holy: I live in a high and holy place.', NOW()),
  ('LOOPS', 'Exodus 26:4', 'Make loops of blue material along the edge of the end curtain in one set, and do the same with the end curtain in the other set.', NOW()),
  ('LORDS', '1 Corinthians 8:5', 'For even if there are so-called gods, whether in heaven or on earth, yet for us there is but one God.', NOW()),
  ('LOVES', 'John 3:16', 'For God so loved the world that he gave his one and only Son, that whoever believes in him shall not perish but have eternal life.', NOW()),
  ('LOWLY', 'Matthew 11:29', 'Take my yoke upon you and learn from me, for I am gentle and lowly in heart, and you will find rest for your souls.', NOW()),
  ('MAKES', 'Psalm 23:2', 'He makes me lie down in green pastures, he leads me beside quiet waters.', NOW()),
  ('MERCY', 'Lamentations 3:22', 'The steadfast love of the LORD never ceases; his mercies never come to an end.', NOW()),
  ('MIGHT', 'Zechariah 4:6', 'Not by might nor by power, but by my Spirit, says the LORD Almighty.', NOW()),
  ('MOVED', 'Acts 2:4', 'All of them were filled with the Holy Spirit and began to speak in other tongues as the Spirit enabled them.', NOW()),
  ('NAMED', 'Isaiah 43:1', 'Do not fear, for I have redeemed you; I have summoned you by name; you are mine.', NOW()),
  ('NEEDS', 'Philippians 4:19', 'And my God will supply every need of yours according to his riches in glory in Christ Jesus.', NOW()),
  ('NIGHT', 'Psalm 139:12', 'Even the darkness will not be dark to you; the night will shine like the day, for darkness is as light to you.', NOW()),
  ('OBEYS', 'John 14:23', 'Jesus replied, Anyone who loves me will obey my teaching. My Father will love them, and we will come to them and make our home with them.', NOW()),
  ('OFFER', 'Romans 12:1', 'I urge you, brothers and sisters, to offer your bodies as a living sacrifice, holy and pleasing to God.', NOW()),
  ('OPENS', 'Revelation 3:8', 'I have placed before you an open door that no one can shut.', NOW()),
  ('OUGHT', 'Romans 8:26', 'We do not know what we ought to pray for, but the Spirit himself intercedes for us through wordless groans.', NOW()),
  ('PAINS', 'Revelation 21:4', 'He will wipe every tear from their eyes. There will be no more death or mourning or crying or pain.', NOW()),
  ('PALMS', 'Revelation 7:9', 'After this I looked, and there before me was a great multitude. They were holding palm branches in their hands.', NOW()),
  ('PATHS', 'Proverbs 3:6', 'In all your ways submit to him, and he will make your paths straight.', NOW()),
  ('PEACE', 'John 14:27', 'Peace I leave with you; my peace I give you. I do not give to you as the world gives.', NOW()),
  ('PEARL', 'Matthew 13:46', 'When he found one of great value, he went away and sold everything he had and bought it.', NOW()),
  ('PERISH', 'John 3:16', 'For God so loved the world that he gave his one and only Son, that whoever believes in him shall not perish.', NOW()),
  ('PLANS', 'Jeremiah 29:11', 'For I know the plans I have for you, declares the LORD, plans to prosper you and not to harm you.', NOW()),
  ('PLANT', 'Isaiah 61:3', 'They will be called oaks of righteousness, a planting of the LORD for the display of his splendor.', NOW()),
  ('POWER', 'Acts 1:8', 'But you will receive power when the Holy Spirit comes on you; and you will be my witnesses.', NOW()),
  ('PRAYS', 'Romans 8:34', 'Christ Jesus who died — more than that, who was raised to life — is at the right hand of God and is also interceding for us.', NOW()),
  ('PRIDE', 'Proverbs 16:18', 'Pride goes before destruction, a haughty spirit before a fall.', NOW()),
  ('PRIZE', 'Philippians 3:14', 'I press on toward the goal to win the prize for which God has called me heavenward in Christ Jesus.', NOW()),
  ('PURGE', 'Psalm 51:7', 'Cleanse me with hyssop, and I will be clean; wash me, and I will be whiter than snow.', NOW()),
  ('QUAKE', 'Psalm 97:4', 'His lightning lights up the world; the earth sees and trembles.', NOW()),
  ('QUEST', 'Matthew 6:33', 'But seek first the kingdom of God and his righteousness.', NOW()),
  ('RAISE', '1 Corinthians 6:14', 'By his power God raised the Lord from the dead, and he will raise us also.', NOW()),
  ('REACH', 'Philippians 3:13', 'Forgetting what is behind and straining toward what is ahead, I press on toward the goal.', NOW()),
  ('READS', 'Revelation 1:3', 'Blessed is the one who reads aloud the words of this prophecy, and blessed are those who hear it and take to heart what is written in it.', NOW()),
  ('REIGN', 'Revelation 11:15', 'The kingdom of the world has become the kingdom of our Lord and of his Messiah, and he will reign for ever and ever.', NOW()),
  ('RENEW', 'Isaiah 40:31', 'But those who hope in the LORD will renew their strength. They will soar on wings like eagles.', NOW()),
  ('REPAY', 'Proverbs 19:17', 'Whoever is kind to the poor lends to the LORD, and he will reward them for what they have done.', NOW()),
  ('RISEN', 'Luke 24:34', 'It is true! The Lord has risen and has appeared to Simon.', NOW()),
  ('RIVER', 'Psalm 46:4', 'There is a river whose streams make glad the city of God, the holy place where the Most High dwells.', NOW()),
  ('ROCKS', 'Matthew 7:24', 'Therefore everyone who hears these words of mine and puts them into practice is like a wise man who built his house on the rock.', NOW()),
  ('ROYAL', '1 Peter 2:9', 'But you are a chosen people, a royal priesthood, a holy nation, God''s special possession.', NOW()),
  ('RULES', 'Psalm 66:7', 'He rules forever by his power, his eyes watch the nations — let not the rebellious rise up against him.', NOW()),
  ('SAVED', 'Ephesians 2:8', 'For it is by grace you have been saved, through faith — and this is not from yourselves, it is the gift of God.', NOW()),
  ('SEALS', 'Ephesians 1:13', 'Having believed, you were marked in him with a seal, the promised Holy Spirit.', NOW()),
  ('SEEKS', 'Luke 15:4', 'Does he not leave the ninety-nine in the open country and go after the lost sheep until he finds it?', NOW()),
  ('SERVE', 'Joshua 24:15', 'But as for me and my household, we will serve the LORD.', NOW()),
  ('SHEEP', 'Psalm 23:1', 'The LORD is my shepherd, I lack nothing.', NOW()),
  ('SHONE', 'Luke 2:9', 'An angel of the Lord appeared to them, and the glory of the Lord shone around them, and they were terrified.', NOW()),
  ('SHOUT', 'Psalm 47:1', 'Clap your hands, all you nations; shout to God with cries of joy.', NOW()),
  ('SHOWN', 'Micah 6:8', 'He has shown you, O mortal, what is good. And what does the LORD require of you?', NOW()),
  ('SIGNS', 'John 20:30', 'Jesus performed many other signs in the presence of his disciples, which are not recorded in this book.', NOW()),
  ('SIMEON', 'Luke 2:25', 'Now there was a man in Jerusalem called Simeon, who was righteous and devout. He was waiting for the consolation of Israel.', NOW()),
  ('SINAI', 'Exodus 19:20', 'The LORD descended to the top of Mount Sinai and called Moses to the top of the mountain.', NOW()),
  ('SINGS', 'Zephaniah 3:17', 'The LORD your God is with you, the Mighty Warrior who saves. He will take great delight in you; he will quiet you with his love, he will rejoice over you with singing.', NOW()),
  ('SMELL', 'Genesis 8:21', 'The LORD smelled the pleasing aroma and said in his heart: Never again will I curse the ground because of humans.', NOW()),
  ('SOLID', '2 Timothy 2:19', 'Nevertheless, God''s solid foundation stands firm, sealed with this inscription: The Lord knows those who are his.', NOW()),
  ('SONGS', 'Colossians 3:16', 'Let the message of Christ dwell among you richly as you teach and admonish one another with all wisdom through psalms, hymns, and songs from the Spirit.', NOW()),
  ('SOWER', 'Matthew 13:3', 'Then he told them many things in parables, saying: A farmer went out to sow his seed.', NOW()),
  ('SPEAK', 'Numbers 22:38', 'I must speak only what God puts in my mouth.', NOW()),
  ('SPEED', 'Psalm 147:15', 'He sends his command to the earth; his word runs swiftly.', NOW()),
  ('SPENT', 'Isaiah 49:4', 'But I said, I have labored in vain; I have spent my strength for nothing at all. Yet what is due me is in the LORD''s hand.', NOW()),
  ('SPINE', 'Job 40:18', 'His bones are like bronze; his ribs are like rods of iron.', NOW()),
  ('SPOKE', 'Hebrews 1:1', 'In the past God spoke to our ancestors through the prophets at many times and in various ways.', NOW()),
  ('STAFF', 'Psalm 23:4', 'Even though I walk through the darkest valley, I will fear no evil, for you are with me; your rod and your staff, they comfort me.', NOW()),
  ('STAND', 'Ephesians 6:13', 'Therefore put on the full armor of God, so that when the day of evil comes, you may be able to stand your ground.', NOW()),
  ('STERN', 'Jonah 1:5', 'The sailors were afraid and each cried out to his own god. And they threw the cargo into the sea to lighten the ship. But Jonah had gone below deck, where he lay down and fell into a deep sleep.', NOW()),
  ('STILL', 'Psalm 46:10', 'He says, Be still, and know that I am God; I will be exalted among the nations, I will be exalted in the earth.', NOW()),
  ('STONE', 'Matthew 21:42', 'The stone the builders rejected has become the cornerstone; the Lord has done this, and it is marvelous in our eyes.', NOW()),
  ('STORE', 'Matthew 6:20', 'But store up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where moths and vermin do not destroy, and where thieves do not break in and steal.', NOW()),
  ('STORM', 'Mark 4:39', 'He got up, rebuked the wind and said to the waves, Quiet! Be still! Then the wind died down and it was completely calm.', NOW()),
  ('STRAY', 'Isaiah 53:6', 'We all, like sheep, have gone astray, each of us has turned to our own way; and the LORD has laid on him the iniquity of us all.', NOW()),
  ('SWEAR', 'Matthew 5:34', 'But I tell you, do not swear an oath at all: either by heaven, for it is God''s throne.', NOW()),
  ('SWEET', 'Psalm 119:103', 'How sweet are your words to my taste, sweeter than honey to my mouth!', NOW()),
  ('SWORD', 'Hebrews 4:12', 'For the word of God is alive and active. Sharper than any double-edged sword, it penetrates even to dividing soul and spirit.', NOW()),
  ('TASTE', 'Psalm 34:8', 'Taste and see that the LORD is good; blessed is the one who takes refuge in him.', NOW()),
  ('TEACH', 'Psalm 25:4', 'Show me your ways, LORD, teach me your paths.', NOW()),
  ('TEARS', 'Psalm 56:8', 'You have kept count of my tossings; put my tears in your bottle.', NOW()),
  ('TENDS', 'Isaiah 40:11', 'He tends his flock like a shepherd: He gathers the lambs in his arms and carries them close to his heart.', NOW()),
  ('TESTS', 'James 1:3', 'Because you know that the testing of your faith produces perseverance.', NOW()),
  ('THANK', 'Psalm 136:1', 'Give thanks to the LORD, for he is good. His love endures forever.', NOW()),
  ('THREE', 'Matthew 18:20', 'For where two or three gather in my name, there am I with them.', NOW()),
  ('THROW', 'Psalm 55:22', 'Cast your cares on the LORD and he will sustain you; he will never let the righteous be shaken.', NOW()),
  ('TIMES', 'Ecclesiastes 3:1', 'There is a time for everything, and a season for every activity under the heavens.', NOW()),
  ('TODAY', 'Hebrews 3:15', 'As has just been said: Today, if you hear his voice, do not harden your hearts.', NOW()),
  ('TOWNS', 'Luke 8:1', 'After this, Jesus traveled about from one town and village to another, proclaiming the good news of the kingdom of God.', NOW()),
  ('TRIBE', 'Revelation 5:5', 'See, the Lion of the tribe of Judah, the Root of David, has triumphed.', NOW()),
  ('TRIED', 'Job 23:10', 'But he knows the way that I take; when he has tested me, I will come forth as gold.', NOW()),
  ('TRIMS', 'John 15:2', 'He cuts off every branch in me that bears no fruit, while every branch that does bear fruit he prunes so that it will be even more fruitful.', NOW()),
  ('TRUST', 'Proverbs 3:5', 'Trust in the LORD with all your heart and lean not on your own understanding.', NOW()),
  ('TRUTH', 'John 8:32', 'Then you will know the truth, and the truth will set you free.', NOW()),
  ('TURNS', 'Proverbs 15:1', 'A gentle answer turns away wrath, but a harsh word stirs up anger.', NOW()),
  ('UNION', 'John 17:21', 'That all of them may be one, Father, just as you are in me and I am in you.', NOW()),
  ('UNITY', 'Ephesians 4:3', 'Make every effort to keep the unity of the Spirit through the bond of peace.', NOW()),
  ('URGED', 'Acts 2:40', 'With many other words he warned them; and he pleaded with them, Save yourselves from this corrupt generation.', NOW()),
  ('VALOR', 'Ruth 3:11', 'All the people of my town know that you are a woman of noble character.', NOW()),
  ('VOICE', 'John 10:27', 'My sheep listen to my voice; I know them, and they follow me.', NOW()),
  ('VOWED', 'Numbers 30:2', 'When a man makes a vow to the LORD or takes an oath to obligate himself by a pledge, he must not break his word.', NOW()),
  ('WALKS', 'Genesis 5:24', 'Enoch walked faithfully with God; then he was no more, because God took him away.', NOW()),
  ('WALLS', 'Nehemiah 4:6', 'So we rebuilt the wall till all of it reached half its height, for the people worked with all their heart.', NOW()),
  ('WATCH', 'Mark 13:37', 'What I say to you, I say to everyone: Watch!', NOW()),
  ('WATER', 'John 4:14', 'But whoever drinks the water I give them will never thirst. Indeed, the water I give them will become in them a spring of water welling up to eternal life.', NOW()),
  ('WAVES', 'Matthew 14:29', 'Then Peter got down out of the boat, walked on the water and came toward Jesus.', NOW()),
  ('WHEAT', 'Matthew 13:30', 'Let both grow together until the harvest. At that time I will tell the harvesters: First collect the weeds and tie them in bundles to be burned; then gather the wheat.', NOW()),
  ('WHOLE', 'Mark 12:30', 'Love the Lord your God with all your heart and with all your soul and with all your mind and with all your strength.', NOW()),
  ('WINDS', 'Psalm 148:8', 'Lightning and hail, snow and clouds, stormy winds that do his bidding.', NOW()),
  ('WINGS', 'Psalm 91:4', 'He will cover you with his feathers, and under his wings you will find refuge.', NOW()),
  ('WORKS', 'James 2:17', 'Faith by itself, if it is not accompanied by action, is dead.', NOW()),
  ('WORLD', 'John 1:10', 'He was in the world, and though the world was made through him, the world did not recognize him.', NOW()),
  ('WRATH', 'Romans 1:18', 'The wrath of God is being revealed from heaven against all the godlessness and wickedness of people.', NOW()),
  ('YIELD', 'Hebrews 12:11', 'No discipline seems pleasant at the time, but painful. Later on, however, it produces a harvest of righteousness and peace.', NOW()),
  ('YOUNG', 'Psalm 119:9', 'How can a young person stay on the path of purity? By living according to your word.', NOW()),
  ('YOURS', 'Psalm 24:1', 'The earth is the LORD''s, and everything in it, the world, and all who live in it.', NOW()),
  ('ZEAL', 'Romans 12:11', 'Never be lacking in zeal, but keep your spiritual fervor, serving the Lord.', NOW())
ON CONFLICT (word) DO NOTHING;

-- M-02 batch 3: additional biblical names, places, and spiritual words to reach 1000+.
INSERT INTO manna_words (word, scripture_reference, scripture_text, created_at) VALUES
  -- Names
  ('BALAK', 'Numbers 22:4', 'So Balak son of Zippor, who was king of Moab at that time, sent messengers to summon Balaam son of Beor.', NOW()),
  ('DINAH', 'Genesis 30:21', 'Some time later she gave birth to a daughter and named her Dinah.', NOW()),
  ('HAMAN', 'Esther 3:5', 'When Haman saw that Mordecai would not kneel down or pay him honor, he was enraged.', NOW()),
  ('JARED', 'Genesis 5:20', 'Altogether, Jared lived a total of 962 years, and then he died.', NOW()),
  ('JORAM', '2 Kings 9:24', 'Then Jehu drew his bow and shot Joram between the shoulders. The arrow pierced his heart and he slumped down in his chariot.', NOW()),
  ('JUNIA', 'Romans 16:7', 'Greet Andronicus and Junia, my fellow Jews who have been in prison with me. They are outstanding among the apostles.', NOW()),
  ('MAGOG', 'Revelation 20:8', 'He will go out to deceive the nations in the four corners of the earth — Gog and Magog — and to gather them for battle.', NOW()),
  ('ORPAH', 'Ruth 1:14', 'At this they wept aloud again. Then Orpah kissed her mother-in-law goodbye, but Ruth clung to her.', NOW()),
  ('PELEG', 'Genesis 10:25', 'Two sons were born to Eber: One was named Peleg, because in his time the earth was divided.', NOW()),
  ('PERGA', 'Acts 13:13', 'From Paphos, Paul and his companions sailed to Perga in Pamphylia, where John left them to return to Jerusalem.', NOW()),
  ('RHODA', 'Acts 12:13', 'Peter knocked at the outer entrance, and a servant named Rhoda came to answer the door.', NOW()),
  ('SELAH', 'Psalm 46:3', 'Though its waters roar and foam and the mountains quake with their surging — Selah.', NOW()),
  ('SHEBA', '1 Kings 10:1', 'When the queen of Sheba heard about the fame of Solomon and his relationship to the LORD, she came to test Solomon with hard questions.', NOW()),
  ('SIDON', 'Matthew 11:21', 'Woe to you, Chorazin! Woe to you, Bethsaida! For if the miracles that were performed in you had been performed in Tyre and Sidon, they would have repented long ago.', NOW()),
  ('TUBAL', 'Ezekiel 38:2', 'Son of man, set your face against Gog, of the land of Magog, the chief prince of Meshek and Tubal; prophesy against him.', NOW()),
  ('TYRUS', 'Ezekiel 27:2', 'Son of man, take up a lament concerning Tyre.', NOW()),
  ('UZZAH', '2 Samuel 6:7', 'The LORD''s anger burned against Uzzah because of his irreverent act; therefore God struck him down, and he died there beside the ark of God.', NOW()),
  ('ZELAH', '2 Samuel 21:14', 'They buried the bones of Saul and his son Jonathan in the tomb of Saul''s father Kish, at Zelah in Benjamin.', NOW()),
  ('ZERAH', 'Genesis 38:30', 'Then his brother, who had the scarlet thread on his wrist, came out. And he was named Zerah.', NOW()),
  ('ZENAS', 'Titus 3:13', 'Do everything you can to help Zenas the lawyer and Apollos on their way and see that they have everything they need.', NOW()),
  ('NAHUM', 'Nahum 1:7', 'The LORD is good, a refuge in times of trouble. He cares for those who trust in him.', NOW()),
  ('CHLOE', '1 Corinthians 1:11', 'My brothers and sisters, some from Chloe''s household have informed me that there are quarrels among you.', NOW()),
  ('LINUS', '2 Timothy 4:21', 'Do your best to get here before winter. Eubulus greets you, and so do Pudens, Linus, Claudia and all the brothers and sisters.', NOW()),
  ('DEBIR', 'Joshua 10:38', 'Then Joshua and all Israel with him turned around and attacked Debir. They took the city, its king and its villages.', NOW()),
  ('CARMI', 'Numbers 26:6', 'Through Carmi, the Carmite clan.', NOW()),
  ('EPHAH', 'Ruth 2:17', 'So Ruth gleaned in the field until evening. Then she threshed the barley she had gathered, and it amounted to about an ephah.', NOW()),
  ('KENAN', 'Genesis 5:12', 'When Kenan had lived 70 years, he became the father of Mahalalel.', NOW()),
  ('IBZAN', 'Judges 12:8', 'After him, Ibzan of Bethlehem led Israel.', NOW()),
  ('IMMER', 'Nehemiah 7:40', 'The descendants of Immer 1,052.', NOW()),
  ('MAHLI', 'Numbers 3:20', 'The Merarite clans: Mahli and Mushi. These were the Levite clans, listed by their families.', NOW()),
  ('PARAN', 'Habakkuk 3:3', 'God came from Teman, the Holy One from Mount Paran. His glory covered the heavens and his praise filled the earth.', NOW()),
  ('SERAH', 'Numbers 26:46', 'And Asher''s daughter was Serah.', NOW()),
  ('TIMNA', 'Genesis 36:22', 'Lotan''s sister was Timna.', NOW()),
  ('ZAHAM', '2 Chronicles 11:19', 'Who bore him Jeush, Shemariah and Zaham.', NOW()),
  ('ZOBAH', '1 Samuel 14:47', 'After Saul had assumed rule over Israel, he fought against their enemies on every side: Moab, the Ammonites, Edom, the kings of Zobah.', NOW()),
  ('KENAZ', 'Judges 3:9', 'But when they cried out to the LORD, he raised up for them a deliverer, Othniel son of Kenaz, Caleb''s younger brother, who saved them.', NOW()),
  ('NOGAH', '1 Chronicles 3:7', 'Nogah, Nepheg, Japhia.', NOW()),
  ('TIRAS', 'Genesis 10:2', 'The sons of Japheth: Gomer, Magog, Madai, Javan, Tubal, Meshek and Tiras.', NOW()),
  ('SHEMA', 'Deuteronomy 6:4', 'Hear, O Israel: The LORD our God, the LORD is one.', NOW()),
  ('SHETH', 'Numbers 24:17', 'A star will come out of Jacob; a scepter will rise out of Israel. He will crush the foreheads of Moab, the skulls of all the people of Sheth.', NOW()),
  ('PURIM', 'Esther 9:26', 'These days were called Purim, from the word pur. Therefore because of everything written in this letter and because of what they had seen and what had happened to them.', NOW()),
  ('SALEM', 'Genesis 14:18', 'Then Melchizedek king of Salem brought out bread and wine. He was priest of God Most High.', NOW()),
  ('SYRIA', 'Luke 2:2', 'This was the first census that took place while Quirinius was governor of Syria.', NOW()),
  ('HIRAM', '1 Kings 7:13', 'King Solomon sent to Tyre and brought Hiram, whose mother was a widow from the tribe of Naphtali and whose father was from Tyre and a skilled craftsman in bronze.', NOW()),
  ('SILAS', 'Acts 16:25', 'About midnight Paul and Silas were praying and singing hymns to God, and the other prisoners were listening to them.', NOW()),
  ('AGABU', 'Acts 21:10', 'After we had been there a number of days, a prophet named Agabus came down from Judea.', NOW()),
  ('TYCHICUS', 'Ephesians 6:21', 'Tychicus, the dear brother and faithful servant in the Lord, will tell you everything.', NOW()),
  ('ONESIMUS', 'Philemon 1:10', 'I appeal to you for my son Onesimus, who became my son while I was in chains.', NOW()),
  -- Places
  ('ASSOS', 'Acts 20:13', 'We went on ahead to the ship and sailed for Assos, where we were going to take Paul aboard.', NOW()),
  ('MYSIA', 'Acts 16:7', 'When they came to the border of Mysia, they tried to enter Bithynia, but the Spirit of Jesus would not allow them to.', NOW()),
  ('ACHAZ', 'Matthew 1:9', 'Jotham the father of Ahaz, Ahaz the father of Hezekiah.', NOW()),
  ('ZOHAR', 'Genesis 23:8', 'He said to them, If you are willing to let me bury my dead, then listen to me and intercede with Ephron son of Zohar on my behalf.', NOW()),
  ('LAISH', 'Judges 18:7', 'So the five men left and came to Laish, where they saw that the people were living in safety, like the Sidonians.', NOW()),
  ('ACHOR', 'Joshua 7:26', 'They raised a large pile of rocks over Achan, which remains to this day. Then the LORD turned from his fierce anger. Therefore that place has been called the Valley of Achor ever since.', NOW()),
  ('SARON', 'Acts 9:35', 'All those who lived in Lydda and Sharon saw him and turned to the Lord.', NOW()),
  ('SEIR', 'Genesis 32:3', 'Jacob sent messengers ahead of him to his brother Esau in the land of Seir, the country of Edom.', NOW()),
  -- Spiritual/theological words
  ('AGREE', 'Matthew 18:19', 'Again, truly I tell you that if two of you on earth agree about anything they ask for, it will be done for them by my Father in heaven.', NOW()),
